  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1250 AM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nOur 2-day warming trend peaks on Saturday with highs in the mid to \nupper 60s to lower 70s south of the Red River.  Another upper wave \noriginating from the Pacific-Northwest will be digging across the \nNorthwestern U.S. on Saturday and through the Great Plains on Sunday \npushing our next cold front through.  Expecting our forecast area to \nstay dry from this system with a \"cold\" rain precipitation staying \nto the north across the Central Plains/Kansas.  Not expecting any \nstrong cold air behind Sundays frontal passage into Oklahoma with \nthe coldest air lagging further north in the Great Plains through \nUpper-Midwest.  Still could see a 10 degree cooldown from Saturday \non Sunday with highs in the 50s.  Deterministic models agree with \nSundays frontal passage although differ with the timing and dynamic \nstrength.  ECMWF is the fastest pushing it through late Saturday \nevening and strongest/windiest while the GFS is slower and weaker \nbringing it through early Sunday morning.  South winds make a second \nreturn on Monday with temperatures rebounding to near seasonably \naverage early next week with another weak & dry upper wave coming \nthrough Tuesday pushing another surface front although weak across \nour area.",
